# The C structs the binding defines for Postgres to allocate (design item 17), one per line, tab-separated: its name,
# its members, each a C declaration, separated by "; ", and what it is. Only the bodies of `calls.list`'s wrappers
# name a struct's members.

DoltgresSlot	VirtualTupleTableSlot base; char *buffer; size_t used; size_t allocated; size_t keyed_len; size_t key_len; size_t tuple_len; size_t values_len; size_t transform_len; int filled; uint64 writer; uint64 deleter; CommandId command; CommandId deleter_command; Oid toast	the fork's tuple table slot: Postgres' virtual slot, which it is while it holds values the executor put in it, then the buffer the slot owns in its memory context, which holds a stored row's key columns, key, tuple, the value ids of its values out of line, and the transform its read takes it through, empty for a row at its reader's epoch, and after them the values of the attributes set so far that are passed by reference, how much of the buffer is used and allocated, the lengths of the key columns, the key, the tuple, the value ids, and the transform, a stored row's tuple being never empty, how many attributes the fork has set, and the version of the stored row or of the row just written from its values, the writer's zero for none: its writer's and its deleter's full xids, the deleter's zero for none, and their commands, and the TOAST relation its values out of line are in
DoltgresScan	TableScanDescData base; DgOwned owned; DgOwned kept; ParallelBlockTableScanWorkerData worker	the fork's table scan: Postgres' scan descriptor, then the handle of the owned record the scan reads through, zero until scan_set_record sets it, then the handle of the owned record its bitmap fetches keep their base in (bugs row 478), zero until scan_set_kept sets it, then a parallel scan worker's chunk of blocks, zero until its first request
DoltgresParallelScan	ParallelBlockTableScanDescData base; DgParallelBase parts; uint32 used; char splits[16384]	the fork's parallel scan: Postgres' block-based parallel scan, which the workers' block counter and its lock live in, then the base every worker reads: the storage's table tree, tuple id tree, and chain tree, the count of its entries, its fresh end, its fold point, and its epoch, which the leader stores before any worker starts; then, for a storage with no base, the delta's split keys the units divide its keys by, as many bytes as used of a fixed budget, which the leader stores at the scan's initialization and its rescan
DoltgresIndexFetch	IndexFetchTableData base; DgBytes key; uint64 copy; DgOwned owned	the fork's index fetch: Postgres' descriptor, then the row key the fork's index method last named, copied into the memory context the fetch was made in and empty until it names one, the tuple id of the copy it names of a row of a table without a primary key, zero for any other, then the handle of the owned record its fetches keep their base in (bugs row 478), zero until fetch_set_record sets it
DoltgresOldEntries	MemoryContext context; int count; bool others; Oid *oids; Relation *indexes; IndexInfo **infos; EState *estate; Datum values[INDEX_MAX_KEYS]; bool isnull[INDEX_MAX_KEYS]	a table's removal of old entries (the btree text's D2b): its memory context, NULL while its slot is free, the table's indexes the fork stores, each one's object id, its relation while a call has it open, and its IndexInfo, whether the table has any other index, the executor state its expressions and predicates run in, and the values its last form made
DoltgresBuild	EState *estate; ExprState *predicate; Datum values[INDEX_MAX_KEYS]; bool isnull[INDEX_MAX_KEYS]	an index build's state over its table's rows: the executor state its expressions run in, its predicate's state, and the values its last row formed
DoltgresSort	Tuplesortstate *state; bytea *current; TupleDesc desc; TupleTableSlot *put; TupleTableSlot *slot	an index build's sort of its entries' bytes: Postgres' tuplesort over byte strings, or for a tree ordered by a comparator over tuples of the entry's key columns' values, then its key's bytes after its key columns, which the tree's comparator ties class-equal keys by, and then its bytes, the value its last next copied out, and the descriptor of those tuples, the virtual slot each one is put through, and the slot each one is read back into, NULL for a sort of bytes alone
DoltgresIndexScan	BTScanOpaqueData base; DgOwned owned; MemoryContext context; MemoryContext entry; FmgrInfo starts[INDEX_MAX_KEYS]	the fork's btree scan state: nbtree's, which _bt_preprocess_keys preprocesses the scan's keys into, then the handle of the owned record the scan reads through, zero until index_scan_set_record sets it, the memory context the scan was made in, the memory context an entry's decoded values live in, reset for each entry, and the ordering functions of a search's start keys, by column
DoltgresIndexParallel	slock_t mutex; bool based; uint32 next; uint32 used; char splits[16384]	the fork's part of a parallel btree scan's shared memory: the spinlock its fields are read and written under, whether a participant stored the units' split keys, the next unit a participant takes, and the split keys' bytes, as many used of a budget the size of the fork's parallel table scan's
